[soh@shiva.trl.oz (kam hung soh) writes:]
[] What is the trick to casting spells?  I have no trouble reading /
[] transcribing the damned books (frustration showing here) but when I
[] want to cast some useful spell, I "goof up".  What sort of attributes
[] do I need to be a successful spellcaster?  What do the numbers next to
[] each spell in mean?  For example, when I was a priest with wisdom 18,
[] power 42, I had no trouble with "light (1)" and "magic missile (2)"
[] spells, but when it comes to something like "identify (5)", I always
[] fail.

nethack 3.0 ...

the numbers next to the spell are the level of the spell.  the higher
the spell level the less likely your success at casting it unless you're
extremely lucky or very smart.  in any event, you also have to be
thinking clearly at the time you cast the spell.

normally your energy points are decreased by the spell level when you
cast a spell but other effects are possible.

